{"beat": 11, "name": "THE ARITHMETIC OF A NICKEL", "text": "Now the mechanism, because it's the opposite of how most businesses set a price. Most start with a cost and add a margin. Woolworth started with the price and worked backwards. His first cost list priced its goods by the gross, 144 items. At a nickel each, a gross brought in $7.20. That figure was fixed. It sat over everything like a ceiling. So every line on his first cost list was really the same question: what does a gross cost? Toy dustpans: $4.75 a gross, which kept about 34% of the price. Animal soap: $5.85 a gross, keeping about 19%. Skimmers and alphabet plates: $2.50 a gross, keeping about 65%. The price never changed. The margin changed on every line.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "Now", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.22}, {"word": "the", "start": 0.22, "end": 0.42}, {"word": "mechanism,", "start": 0.42, "end": 0.9}, {"word": "because", "start": 0.9, "end": 1.22}, {"word": "it's", "start": 1.22, "end": 1.46}, {"word": "the", "start": 1.46, "end": 1.6}, {"word": "opposite", "start": 1.6, "end": 2.02}, {"word": "of", "start": 2.02, "end": 2.24}, {"word": "how", "start": 2.24, "end": 2.4}, {"word": "most", "start": 2.4, "end": 2.68}, {"word": "businesses", "start": 2.68, "end": 3.18}, {"word": "set", "start": 3.18, "end": 3.5}, {"word": "a", "start": 3.5, "end": 3.62}, {"word": "price.", "start": 3.62, "end": 3.98}, {"word": "Most", "start": 4.56, "end": 4.76}, {"word": "start", "start": 4.76, "end": 5.06}, {"word": "with", "start": 5.06, "end": 5.22}, {"word": "a", "start": 5.22, "end": 5.34}, {"word": "cost", "start": 5.34, "end": 5.7}, {"word": "and", "start": 5.7, "end": 5.94}, {"word": "add", "start": 5.94, "end": 6.2}, {"word": "a", "start": 6.2, "end": 6.28}, {"word": "margin.", "start": 6.28, "end": 6.72}, {"word": "Woolworth", "start": 7.44, "end": 7.8}, {"word": "started", "start": 7.8, "end": 8.16}, {"word": "with", "start": 8.16, "end": 8.38}, {"word": "the", "start": 8.38, "end